    "summary": "High‑energy August ’71 Bronx show with smoking Hard To Handle and rare Empty Pages",
    "blurb": "The set bursts open with a scorching Hard To Handle and the only known live Pigpen vocal on Empty Pages. A powerful second‑set The Other One jam leads into a tight Saint Stephen > Not Fade Away sequence. Soundboard sources capture most of the performance with good clarity despite occasional tape quirks.",
    "review": "August 26, 1971 at Gaelic Park finds the Dead riding a wave of raw, outdoor intensity that still feels fresh today. The first set swings from a rousing Bertha into a blistering Hard To Handle, then delivers Pigpen’s haunting rendition of Empty Pages – his last show for three months and only the second ever recorded. Jerry’s guitar cuts through the mix, soaring on solos and even surviving a brief string break during Rider, while Phil’s “elephant‑step” bass propels the band forward with thunderous lows. The second set builds momentum with a classic Truckin' into drums, then erupts into an expansive The Other One that captures the raunchy early‑70s vibe. The climax arrives in a seamless Saint Stephen > Not Fade Away > Goin’ Down the Road Feeling Bad medley, showcasing tight interplay and inspired improvisation. Although some tape drop‑outs linger on the fair‑quality SBD, the patched Miller soundboard version preserves the show’s energy with remarkable balance and fidelity.",
